-- title:
--   Faithfully flat lift family from Artinian lifting property
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring of finite type over $\mathbb{Z}$, let $n \in \mathbb{N}$, write $P =$ `MvPolynomial (Fin n) R` for the polynomial ring $R[x_1,\dots,x_n]$, and let $I \le J$ be ideals of $P$ with $J$ maximal. Assume the following lifting hypothesis: for every commutative local Artinian ring $T'$ whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $\ell$ for some prime $\ell$, every nontrivial commutative ring $T$, any $R$-algebra structures on $T'$ and $T$, and every surjective $R$-algebra map $p : T' \to T$ whose kernel satisfies $(\ker p)\cdot \mathfrak{m}_{T'} = 0$, every $R$-algebra map $m : P/I \to T$ admits an $R$-algebra map $m' : P/I \to T'$ with $p \circ m' = m$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a family of types $D(N)$ indexed by $N \in \mathbb{N}$, together with, for each $N$, a commutative ring structure on $D(N)$, an $R$-algebra structure, an algebra structure over $C_N := P/(J^N + J I)$ compatible with the $R$-structure as a scalar tower $R \to C_N \to D(N)$, and faithful flatness of $D(N)$ as a $C_N$-module, and of $R$-algebra maps $\sigma_N : P/I \to D(N)$ such that for every $N$ and every $f \in P$ the difference between $\sigma_N(f \bmod I)$ and the image in $D(N)$ of $f \bmod (J^N + JI)$ lies in the ideal of $D(N)$ generated by the image of $J^N + I$ in $C_N$.
--
--   This packages the infinitesimal lifting property against small surjections of Artin local algebras with algebraically closed residue field into exactly the data — a faithfully flat extension $D(N)$ of $P/(J^N + JI)$ together with an approximate $R$-algebra lift $\sigma_N$ of $P/I$ — required by the Jacobian-criterion step. It is used in the proof of smoothness from the lifting property for Artinian test algebras, [`AlgebraicGeometry.Smooth.of_forall_exists_lift_of_isArtinianRing_of_charP_of_finiteType_int`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Smooth.of_forall_exists_lift_of_isArtinianRing_of_charP_of_finiteType_int), and relies on the finiteness of residue fields at maximal ideals of finite-type $\mathbb{Z}$-algebras together with the existence of a faithfully flat unramified Artin local extension with algebraically closed residue field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPolynomial_exists_faithfullyFlat_algHom_lift_family_of_forall_isArtinianRing_exists_algHom_lift.lean

